IMPORT prelude
IMPORT `qira-dates`
IMPORT `qira-claims`

-- Industrial Relations Act 2016 (Qld) -- the claims an employee meets, from the seat of the employee.
--
-- SEAT: the employee (or former employee) bringing or weighing a claim against their employer. "Can I claim unfair
-- dismissal? By when must I apply? What can the commission give me? How much notice or redundancy pay am I owed? Can
-- I still recover unpaid wages, and where?" Every question is asked as that person would ask it, on facts that person
-- could state; the commission's judgments are facts the person answers from what they have been told or expect. The
-- rules are in qira-claims.l4; this module builds its records from plain answers and restates no rule. Inputs with the
-- same meaning have the same name in every question, so the form can ask them once.
--
-- BASELINE. Not for public use as advice. See NOTES.md.

§ `Industrial Relations Act 2016 (Qld) -- the employee's questions`

-- A placeholder for a date field that the question's rule does not read (the record needs a value).
`an unused date` MEANS DATE_FROM_DMY 1 1 2000

-- Builds the core's record of one employment from the employee's plain answers.
GIVEN `the day my continuous service started`                                             IS A DATE
      `the day my dismissal takes effect`                                                 IS A DATE
      `my date of birth`                                                                  IS A DATE
      `how I was engaged`                                                                 IS A `Basis of engagement`
      `what was agreed about probation`                                                   IS A `Probation agreement`
      `the agreed probation in months`                                                    IS A NUMBER
      `the longer probation is reasonable`                                                IS A BOOLEAN
      `I was engaged regularly and systematically`                                        IS A BOOLEAN
      `I was engaged for several periods over at least 6 months`                          IS A BOOLEAN
      `I reasonably expected further employment`                                          IS A BOOLEAN
      `the main purpose of my fixed engagement was to avoid unfair dismissal obligations` IS A BOOLEAN
      `I am in a labour market program`                                                   IS A BOOLEAN
      `I was dismissed before the period ended or the task was complete`                  IS A BOOLEAN
      `I am employed under an industrial instrument`                                      IS A BOOLEAN
      `I am a public service officer on tenure`                                           IS A BOOLEAN
      `my annual wages before the dismissal`                                              IS A NUMBER
      `the high income threshold`                                                         IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A `The employment`
`my employment` `the day my continuous service started` `the day my dismissal takes effect` `my date of birth` `how I was engaged` `what was agreed about probation` `the agreed probation in months` `the longer probation is reasonable` `I was engaged regularly and systematically` `I was engaged for several periods over at least 6 months` `I reasonably expected further employment` `the main purpose of my fixed engagement was to avoid unfair dismissal obligations` `I am in a labour market program` `I was dismissed before the period ended or the task was complete` `I am employed under an industrial instrument` `I am a public service officer on tenure` `my annual wages before the dismissal` `the high income threshold` MEANS
    `The employment` WITH
        `the day continuous service started`                   IS `the day my continuous service started`
        `the day the dismissal takes effect`                   IS `the day my dismissal takes effect`
        `the employee's date of birth`                         IS `my date of birth`
        `the basis of engagement`                              IS `how I was engaged`
        `the probation agreement`                              IS `what was agreed about probation`
        `the agreed probation in months`                       IS `the agreed probation in months`
        `the longer probation is a reasonable period`          IS `the longer probation is reasonable`
        `engaged regularly and systematically`                 IS `I was engaged regularly and systematically`
        `engaged for several periods over at least 6 months`   IS `I was engaged for several periods over at least 6 months`
        `had a reasonable expectation of further employment`   IS `I reasonably expected further employment`
        `the main purpose of the fixed engagement was to avoid division 2` IS `the main purpose of my fixed engagement was to avoid unfair dismissal obligations`
        `in a labour market program`                           IS `I am in a labour market program`
        `dismissed before the period ended or the task was complete` IS `I was dismissed before the period ended or the task was complete`
        `employed under an industrial instrument`              IS `I am employed under an industrial instrument`
        `a public service officer employed on tenure`          IS `I am a public service officer on tenure`
        `annual wages immediately before the dismissal`        IS `my annual wages before the dismissal`
        `the high income threshold`                            IS `the high income threshold`

§§ `Unfair dismissal (ss 315-324)`
-- Situation: only if you have been dismissed.

@export Can I claim unfair dismissal against my employer under the Industrial Relations Act 2016 (Qld), or am I one of the employees the unfair dismissal provisions do not cover (s 315)?
GIVEN `the day my continuous service started`                                             IS A DATE @desc The day your continuous service with this employer started, counting service with a former employer that the Act treats as service with this one (s 132), ISO 8601
      `the day my dismissal takes effect`                                                 IS A DATE @desc The day your dismissal took (or takes) effect, ISO 8601
      `how I was engaged`                                                                 IS A `Basis of engagement` @desc How you were engaged: on an ongoing basis, as a casual employee, by the hour or day, for a specific period or task, or for the duration of a particular season
      `what was agreed about probation`                                                   IS A `Probation agreement` @desc What you and your employer agreed in writing about probation: nothing, a shorter probation than 3 months, no probation, or (before you started) a longer probation
      `the agreed probation in months`                                                    IS A NUMBER @desc If you agreed a longer probation, how many months it was (otherwise 0)
      `the longer probation is reasonable`                                                IS A BOOLEAN @desc If you agreed a longer probation: whether it is a reasonable period for the nature and circumstances of the job (a judgment the commission makes; answer as you have been told or expect)
      `I was engaged regularly and systematically`                                        IS A BOOLEAN @desc If casual: whether this employer engaged you on a regular and systematic basis
      `I was engaged for several periods over at least 6 months`                          IS A BOOLEAN @desc If casual: whether you were engaged for several periods of employment over a period of at least 6 months
      `I reasonably expected further employment`                                          IS A BOOLEAN @desc If casual: whether, apart from the employer's decision not to offer you more work, you had a reasonable expectation of further employment
      `the main purpose of my fixed engagement was to avoid unfair dismissal obligations` IS A BOOLEAN @desc If engaged for a specific period or task: whether the main purpose of engaging you that way was to avoid the employer's unfair dismissal obligations (a judgment the commission makes)
      `I am in a labour market program`                                                   IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether you were employed as a participant in a labour market program
      `I was dismissed before the period ended or the task was complete`                  IS A BOOLEAN @desc If engaged for a specific period or task: whether you were dismissed before the period ended or the task was complete
      `I am employed under an industrial instrument`                                      IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether an award, certified agreement or other industrial instrument covers your employment
      `I am a public service officer on tenure`                                           IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether you are a public service officer employed on tenure under the Public Sector Act 2022
      `my annual wages before the dismissal`                                              IS A NUMBER @desc Your annual wages immediately before the dismissal, in Australian dollars
      `the high income threshold`                                                         IS A NUMBER @desc The high income threshold under the Fair Work Act 2009 (Cwlth) s 333 at the time, in Australian dollars a year
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`can I claim unfair dismissal` `the day my continuous service started` `the day my dismissal takes effect` `how I was engaged` `what was agreed about probation` `the agreed probation in months` `the longer probation is reasonable` `I was engaged regularly and systematically` `I was engaged for several periods over at least 6 months` `I reasonably expected further employment` `the main purpose of my fixed engagement was to avoid unfair dismissal obligations` `I am in a labour market program` `I was dismissed before the period ended or the task was complete` `I am employed under an industrial instrument` `I am a public service officer on tenure` `my annual wages before the dismissal` `the high income threshold` MEANS
    `the employee may claim unfair dismissal` (`my employment` `the day my continuous service started` `the day my dismissal takes effect` `an unused date` `how I was engaged` `what was agreed about probation` `the agreed probation in months` `the longer probation is reasonable` `I was engaged regularly and systematically` `I was engaged for several periods over at least 6 months` `I reasonably expected further employment` `the main purpose of my fixed engagement was to avoid unfair dismissal obligations` `I am in a labour market program` `I was dismissed before the period ended or the task was complete` `I am employed under an industrial instrument` `I am a public service officer on tenure` `my annual wages before the dismissal` `the high income threshold`)

@export By when must I apply to the Queensland Industrial Relations Commission for reinstatement after an unfair dismissal (s 317(2))? Later, only if the commission allows a further period.
GIVEN `the day of the dismissal` IS A DATE @desc The day your dismissal took effect, ISO 8601
GIVETH A DATE
`last day to apply for reinstatement` `the day of the dismissal` MEANS
    `the last day to apply for reinstatement` `the day of the dismissal`

@export The registrar rejected my unfair dismissal application as excluded: by when must I give written notice that I want it to proceed (s 317(6))?
GIVEN `the day I received the rejection notice` IS A DATE @desc The day you received the registrar's written notice rejecting your unfair dismissal application, ISO 8601
GIVETH A DATE
`last day to insist my application proceed` `the day I received the rejection notice` MEANS
    `the last day to insist that a rejected application proceed` `the day I received the rejection notice`

@export After the conciliation certificate, by when must I take action on my unfair dismissal application or it lapses (s 318(4))?
GIVEN `the day the commission informed me after conciliation` IS A DATE @desc The day the commission informed you of its assessment after issuing the conciliation certificate (s 318(3)), ISO 8601
GIVETH A DATE
`last day to act after conciliation` `the day the commission informed me after conciliation` MEANS
    `the last day to act on the application after the certificate` `the day the commission informed me after conciliation`

@export Has my unfair dismissal application lapsed because I took no action within 6 months after the conciliation certificate (s 318(4))?
GIVEN `the day the commission informed me after conciliation` IS A DATE @desc The day the commission informed you of its assessment after issuing the conciliation certificate (s 318(3)), ISO 8601
      `I have taken action on the application`                IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether you have since taken any action on the application, or discontinued it
      `the day I first took action`                           IS A DATE @desc If you have, the first day you did so after being informed, ISO 8601 (otherwise any date)
      `today`                                                 IS A DATE @desc The day you are asking about, ISO 8601
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`has my application lapsed` `the day the commission informed me after conciliation` `I have taken action on the application` `the day I first took action` `today` MEANS
    `the application has lapsed` `the day the commission informed me after conciliation` `I have taken action on the application` `the day I first took action` `today`

@export What must the commission consider in deciding whether my dismissal was harsh, unjust or unreasonable, and may it find it fair because of unlawful conduct or harassment at work (s 320)?
GIVEN `what the dismissal related to`                           IS A `What the dismissal related to` @desc What your dismissal related to: the operational requirements of the employer, your conduct, capacity or performance, or something else
      `the conduct was at work or connected with my employment` IS A BOOLEAN @desc If it related to your conduct: whether the conduct was at work or otherwise connected with your employment
      `the conduct was unlawful or harassment`                  IS A BOOLEAN @desc If it related to your conduct: whether the conduct was, wholly or partly, unlawful, or sexual harassment or sex or gender-based harassment
GIVETH A LIST OF `Matter the commission considers`
`what will the commission consider` `what the dismissal related to` `the conduct was at work or connected with my employment` `the conduct was unlawful or harassment` MEANS
    `the matters the commission must consider` `what the dismissal related to` `the conduct was at work or connected with my employment` `the conduct was unlawful or harassment`

@export What is the most compensation the commission can order for my unfair dismissal (s 322)? Compensation is possible only if the commission considers reinstatement or re-employment impracticable.
GIVEN `I am employed under an industrial instrument`         IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether an award, certified agreement or other industrial instrument covers your employment
      `my annual wages before the dismissal`                 IS A NUMBER @desc Your annual wages immediately before the dismissal, in Australian dollars
      `the high income threshold`                            IS A NUMBER @desc The high income threshold under the Fair Work Act 2009 (Cwlth) s 333 at the time, in Australian dollars a year
      `the commission considers reinstatement impracticable` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether the commission considers that reinstating or re-employing you would be impracticable (its judgment)
GIVETH A `Compensation answer`
`most unfair dismissal compensation` `I am employed under an industrial instrument` `my annual wages before the dismissal` `the high income threshold` `the commission considers reinstatement impracticable` MEANS
    `the most unfair dismissal compensation` (`my employment` `an unused date` `an unused date` `an unused date` `engaged on an ongoing basis` `no written agreement about probation` 0 FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE `I am employed under an industrial instrument` FALSE `my annual wages before the dismissal` `the high income threshold`) `the commission considers reinstatement impracticable`

@export If my employer wilfully fails to reinstate or re-employ me as ordered, what is the most extra amount (besides lost wages) the commission can order paid to me (s 323)?
GIVEN `the value of a penalty unit` IS A NUMBER @desc The value of one penalty unit in Queensland at the time, in Australian dollars (set under the Penalties and Sentences Act 1992)
GIVETH A NUMBER
`most extra amount if not reinstated` `the value of a penalty unit` MEANS
    `the most extra amount for a wilful failure to reinstate` `the value of a penalty unit`

§§ `Severance and mass dismissals (ss 325-331)`
-- Situation: only if you have been, or are about to be, dismissed.

@export Do the Act's requirements for dismissal (severance orders, and notice and consultation before a mass dismissal) protect me, or am I excluded (s 315(4), (5), (8))?
GIVEN `the day my continuous service started`                                             IS A DATE @desc The day your continuous service with this employer started, counting service with a former employer that the Act treats as service with this one (s 132), ISO 8601
      `the day my dismissal takes effect`                                                 IS A DATE @desc The day your dismissal took (or takes) effect, ISO 8601
      `how I was engaged`                                                                 IS A `Basis of engagement` @desc How you were engaged: on an ongoing basis, as a casual employee, by the hour or day, for a specific period or task, or for the duration of a particular season
      `what was agreed about probation`                                                   IS A `Probation agreement` @desc What you and your employer agreed in writing about probation: nothing, a shorter probation than 3 months, no probation, or (before you started) a longer probation
      `the agreed probation in months`                                                    IS A NUMBER @desc If you agreed a longer probation, how many months it was (otherwise 0)
      `the longer probation is reasonable`                                                IS A BOOLEAN @desc If you agreed a longer probation: whether it is a reasonable period for the nature and circumstances of the job (a judgment the commission makes; answer as you have been told or expect)
      `I was engaged regularly and systematically`                                        IS A BOOLEAN @desc If casual: whether this employer engaged you on a regular and systematic basis
      `I was engaged for several periods over at least 6 months`                          IS A BOOLEAN @desc If casual: whether you were engaged for several periods of employment over a period of at least 6 months
      `I reasonably expected further employment`                                          IS A BOOLEAN @desc If casual: whether, apart from the employer's decision not to offer you more work, you had a reasonable expectation of further employment
      `the main purpose of my fixed engagement was to avoid unfair dismissal obligations` IS A BOOLEAN @desc If engaged for a specific period or task: whether the main purpose of engaging you that way was to avoid the employer's unfair dismissal obligations (a judgment the commission makes)
      `I am in a labour market program`                                                   IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether you were employed as a participant in a labour market program
      `I was dismissed before the period ended or the task was complete`                  IS A BOOLEAN @desc If engaged for a specific period or task: whether you were dismissed before the period ended or the task was complete
      `I am employed under an industrial instrument`                                      IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether an award, certified agreement or other industrial instrument covers your employment
      `I am a public service officer on tenure`                                           IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether you are a public service officer employed on tenure under the Public Sector Act 2022
      `my annual wages before the dismissal`                                              IS A NUMBER @desc Your annual wages immediately before the dismissal, in Australian dollars
      `the high income threshold`                                                         IS A NUMBER @desc The high income threshold under the Fair Work Act 2009 (Cwlth) s 333 at the time, in Australian dollars a year
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`do the requirements for dismissal protect me` `the day my continuous service started` `the day my dismissal takes effect` `how I was engaged` `what was agreed about probation` `the agreed probation in months` `the longer probation is reasonable` `I was engaged regularly and systematically` `I was engaged for several periods over at least 6 months` `I reasonably expected further employment` `the main purpose of my fixed engagement was to avoid unfair dismissal obligations` `I am in a labour market program` `I was dismissed before the period ended or the task was complete` `I am employed under an industrial instrument` `I am a public service officer on tenure` `my annual wages before the dismissal` `the high income threshold` MEANS
    `division 3 protects the employee` (`my employment` `the day my continuous service started` `the day my dismissal takes effect` `an unused date` `how I was engaged` `what was agreed about probation` `the agreed probation in months` `the longer probation is reasonable` `I was engaged regularly and systematically` `I was engaged for several periods over at least 6 months` `I reasonably expected further employment` `the main purpose of my fixed engagement was to avoid unfair dismissal obligations` `I am in a labour market program` `I was dismissed before the period ended or the task was complete` `I am employed under an industrial instrument` `I am a public service officer on tenure` `my annual wages before the dismissal` `the high income threshold`)

@export By when must I apply for an order about severance allowance, or about an employer's failure to notify or consult before a mass dismissal (ss 327, 331)? I may also apply before the dismissal.
GIVEN `the day of the dismissal` IS A DATE @desc The day your dismissal took effect, ISO 8601
GIVETH A DATE
`last day to apply about severance or a mass dismissal` `the day of the dismissal` MEANS
    `the last day to apply about severance or a mass dismissal` `the day of the dismissal`

@export Did my employer have to notify the Commonwealth employment agency and the unions, and consult the unions, before dismissing me with others (s 328)?
GIVEN `the number of employees to be dismissed`             IS A NUMBER @desc How many employees your employer decided to dismiss
      `for an economic, technological or structural reason` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether the employer decided to dismiss them for an economic, technological or structural reason
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`did my employer have to notify and consult` `the number of employees to be dismissed` `for an economic, technological or structural reason` MEANS
    `subdivision 2 applies to the decision` `the number of employees to be dismissed` `for an economic, technological or structural reason`

@export What is the most the commission can order my employer to pay me for breaching a severance order or failing to notify of a mass dismissal (ss 326(3)(b), 329(3)(c))?
GIVEN `the value of a penalty unit` IS A NUMBER @desc The value of one penalty unit in Queensland at the time, in Australian dollars (set under the Penalties and Sentences Act 1992)
GIVETH A NUMBER
`most payable for a severance or notice breach` `the value of a penalty unit` MEANS
    `the most the employer can be ordered to pay the employee under ss 326 or 329` `the value of a penalty unit`

§§ `Stand-down (ss 332-333)`
-- Situation: only if you have been stood down.

@export I was stood down in December and re-employed in January: which Christmas and New Year public holidays must my employer pay me for at my ordinary rate (s 332)?
GIVEN `I am a casual employee`                   IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether you were a casual employee
      `I am in a labour market program`          IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether you were employed as a participant in a labour market program
      `the day my continuous employment started` IS A DATE @desc The day your continuous period of employment with this employer began, ISO 8601
      `the day I was stood down`                 IS A DATE @desc The day you were stood down or dismissed, ISO 8601
      `the day I was re-employed`                IS A DATE @desc The day you were re-employed by the same employer, ISO 8601
GIVETH A LIST OF `Christmas public holiday`
`which stand-down holidays must I be paid for` `I am a casual employee` `I am in a labour market program` `the day my continuous employment started` `the day I was stood down` `the day I was re-employed` MEANS
    `the stand-down public holidays the employer must pay` `I am a casual employee` `I am in a labour market program` `the day my continuous employment started` `the day I was stood down` `the day I was re-employed`

@export Can my employer stand me down without pay because I cannot be usefully employed (s 333)? No answer (null) means s 333 does not give the permission on these facts.
GIVEN `I can not be usefully employed`                                IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether you cannot be usefully employed on the day
      `the cause is outside the employer's responsibility or control` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether that is because of something the employer is not responsible for or has no control over
      `my industrial instrument provides otherwise`                   IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether an industrial instrument covering you provides otherwise (for example, pay during a stand-down)
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`can I be stood down without pay` `I can not be usefully employed` `the cause is outside the employer's responsibility or control` `my industrial instrument provides otherwise` MEANS
    `s 333 lets the employer stand the employee down without pay` `I can not be usefully employed` `the cause is outside the employer's responsibility or control` `my industrial instrument provides otherwise`

§§ `Notice of termination and redundancy pay (ss 120-127)`
-- Situation: only if your employment is ending.

@export How many weeks' notice of termination must my employer give me under the Industrial Relations Act 2016 (Qld) (ss 120, 123)?
GIVEN `the day my continuous service started`                                             IS A DATE @desc The day your continuous service with this employer started, counting service with a former employer that the Act treats as service with this one (s 132), ISO 8601
      `the day my dismissal takes effect`                                                 IS A DATE @desc The day your dismissal took (or takes) effect, ISO 8601
      `my date of birth`                                                                  IS A DATE @desc Your date of birth, ISO 8601
      `how I was engaged`                                                                 IS A `Basis of engagement` @desc How you were engaged: on an ongoing basis, as a casual employee, by the hour or day, for a specific period or task, or for the duration of a particular season
      `what was agreed about probation`                                                   IS A `Probation agreement` @desc What you and your employer agreed in writing about probation: nothing, a shorter probation than 3 months, no probation, or (before you started) a longer probation
      `the agreed probation in months`                                                    IS A NUMBER @desc If you agreed a longer probation, how many months it was (otherwise 0)
      `the longer probation is reasonable`                                                IS A BOOLEAN @desc If you agreed a longer probation: whether it is a reasonable period for the nature and circumstances of the job (a judgment the commission makes; answer as you have been told or expect)
      `I was engaged regularly and systematically`                                        IS A BOOLEAN @desc If casual: whether this employer engaged you on a regular and systematic basis
      `I was engaged for several periods over at least 6 months`                          IS A BOOLEAN @desc If casual: whether you were engaged for several periods of employment over a period of at least 6 months
      `I reasonably expected further employment`                                          IS A BOOLEAN @desc If casual: whether, apart from the employer's decision not to offer you more work, you had a reasonable expectation of further employment
      `the main purpose of my fixed engagement was to avoid unfair dismissal obligations` IS A BOOLEAN @desc If engaged for a specific period or task: whether the main purpose of engaging you that way was to avoid the employer's unfair dismissal obligations (a judgment the commission makes)
      `I am in a labour market program`                                                   IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether you were employed as a participant in a labour market program
      `I was dismissed before the period ended or the task was complete`                  IS A BOOLEAN @desc If engaged for a specific period or task: whether you were dismissed before the period ended or the task was complete
      `I am employed under an industrial instrument`                                      IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether an award, certified agreement or other industrial instrument covers your employment
      `I am a public service officer on tenure`                                           IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether you are a public service officer employed on tenure under the Public Sector Act 2022
      `my annual wages before the dismissal`                                              IS A NUMBER @desc Your annual wages immediately before the dismissal, in Australian dollars
      `the high income threshold`                                                         IS A NUMBER @desc The high income threshold under the Fair Work Act 2009 (Cwlth) s 333 at the time, in Australian dollars a year
GIVETH A `Notice answer`
`how much notice must I be given` `the day my continuous service started` `the day my dismissal takes effect` `my date of birth` `how I was engaged` `what was agreed about probation` `the agreed probation in months` `the longer probation is reasonable` `I was engaged regularly and systematically` `I was engaged for several periods over at least 6 months` `I reasonably expected further employment` `the main purpose of my fixed engagement was to avoid unfair dismissal obligations` `I am in a labour market program` `I was dismissed before the period ended or the task was complete` `I am employed under an industrial instrument` `I am a public service officer on tenure` `my annual wages before the dismissal` `the high income threshold` MEANS
    `the notice the employer must give` (`my employment` `the day my continuous service started` `the day my dismissal takes effect` `my date of birth` `how I was engaged` `what was agreed about probation` `the agreed probation in months` `the longer probation is reasonable` `I was engaged regularly and systematically` `I was engaged for several periods over at least 6 months` `I reasonably expected further employment` `the main purpose of my fixed engagement was to avoid unfair dismissal obligations` `I am in a labour market program` `I was dismissed before the period ended or the task was complete` `I am employed under an industrial instrument` `I am a public service officer on tenure` `my annual wages before the dismissal` `the high income threshold`)

@export If I am dismissed without notice, what is the least my employer must pay me instead (s 124)?
GIVEN `the day my continuous service started`                                             IS A DATE @desc The day your continuous service with this employer started, counting service with a former employer that the Act treats as service with this one (s 132), ISO 8601
      `the day my dismissal takes effect`                                                 IS A DATE @desc The day your dismissal took (or takes) effect, ISO 8601
      `my date of birth`                                                                  IS A DATE @desc Your date of birth, ISO 8601
      `how I was engaged`                                                                 IS A `Basis of engagement` @desc How you were engaged: on an ongoing basis, as a casual employee, by the hour or day, for a specific period or task, or for the duration of a particular season
      `what was agreed about probation`                                                   IS A `Probation agreement` @desc What you and your employer agreed in writing about probation: nothing, a shorter probation than 3 months, no probation, or (before you started) a longer probation
      `the agreed probation in months`                                                    IS A NUMBER @desc If you agreed a longer probation, how many months it was (otherwise 0)
      `the longer probation is reasonable`                                                IS A BOOLEAN @desc If you agreed a longer probation: whether it is a reasonable period for the nature and circumstances of the job (a judgment the commission makes; answer as you have been told or expect)
      `I was engaged regularly and systematically`                                        IS A BOOLEAN @desc If casual: whether this employer engaged you on a regular and systematic basis
      `I was engaged for several periods over at least 6 months`                          IS A BOOLEAN @desc If casual: whether you were engaged for several periods of employment over a period of at least 6 months
      `I reasonably expected further employment`                                          IS A BOOLEAN @desc If casual: whether, apart from the employer's decision not to offer you more work, you had a reasonable expectation of further employment
      `the main purpose of my fixed engagement was to avoid unfair dismissal obligations` IS A BOOLEAN @desc If engaged for a specific period or task: whether the main purpose of engaging you that way was to avoid the employer's unfair dismissal obligations (a judgment the commission makes)
      `I am in a labour market program`                                                   IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether you were employed as a participant in a labour market program
      `I was dismissed before the period ended or the task was complete`                  IS A BOOLEAN @desc If engaged for a specific period or task: whether you were dismissed before the period ended or the task was complete
      `I am employed under an industrial instrument`                                      IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether an award, certified agreement or other industrial instrument covers your employment
      `I am a public service officer on tenure`                                           IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether you are a public service officer employed on tenure under the Public Sector Act 2022
      `my annual wages before the dismissal`                                              IS A NUMBER @desc Your annual wages immediately before the dismissal, in Australian dollars
      `the high income threshold`                                                         IS A NUMBER @desc The high income threshold under the Fair Work Act 2009 (Cwlth) s 333 at the time, in Australian dollars a year
      `my weekly pay for ordinary hours`                                                  IS A NUMBER @desc Your pay for a week of your ordinary hours, including allowances, loadings and penalties and other amounts under your contract, in Australian dollars
GIVETH A `Pay in lieu answer`
`least pay instead of notice` `the day my continuous service started` `the day my dismissal takes effect` `my date of birth` `how I was engaged` `what was agreed about probation` `the agreed probation in months` `the longer probation is reasonable` `I was engaged regularly and systematically` `I was engaged for several periods over at least 6 months` `I reasonably expected further employment` `the main purpose of my fixed engagement was to avoid unfair dismissal obligations` `I am in a labour market program` `I was dismissed before the period ended or the task was complete` `I am employed under an industrial instrument` `I am a public service officer on tenure` `my annual wages before the dismissal` `the high income threshold` `my weekly pay for ordinary hours` MEANS
    `the minimum compensation instead of notice` (`my employment` `the day my continuous service started` `the day my dismissal takes effect` `my date of birth` `how I was engaged` `what was agreed about probation` `the agreed probation in months` `the longer probation is reasonable` `I was engaged regularly and systematically` `I was engaged for several periods over at least 6 months` `I reasonably expected further employment` `the main purpose of my fixed engagement was to avoid unfair dismissal obligations` `I am in a labour market program` `I was dismissed before the period ended or the task was complete` `I am employed under an industrial instrument` `I am a public service officer on tenure` `my annual wages before the dismissal` `the high income threshold`) `my weekly pay for ordinary hours`

@export Can my employer dismiss me without notice or pay instead of notice because of my misconduct (s 121)? No answer (null) means the Act leaves it open on these facts, or the notice rules do not apply to me.
GIVEN `the day my continuous service started`                                             IS A DATE @desc The day your continuous service with this employer started, counting service with a former employer that the Act treats as service with this one (s 132), ISO 8601
      `the day my dismissal takes effect`                                                 IS A DATE @desc The day your dismissal took (or takes) effect, ISO 8601
      `how I was engaged`                                                                 IS A `Basis of engagement` @desc How you were engaged: on an ongoing basis, as a casual employee, by the hour or day, for a specific period or task, or for the duration of a particular season
      `what was agreed about probation`                                                   IS A `Probation agreement` @desc What you and your employer agreed in writing about probation: nothing, a shorter probation than 3 months, no probation, or (before you started) a longer probation
      `the agreed probation in months`                                                    IS A NUMBER @desc If you agreed a longer probation, how many months it was (otherwise 0)
      `the longer probation is reasonable`                                                IS A BOOLEAN @desc If you agreed a longer probation: whether it is a reasonable period for the nature and circumstances of the job (a judgment the commission makes; answer as you have been told or expect)
      `I was engaged regularly and systematically`                                        IS A BOOLEAN @desc If casual: whether this employer engaged you on a regular and systematic basis
      `I was engaged for several periods over at least 6 months`                          IS A BOOLEAN @desc If casual: whether you were engaged for several periods of employment over a period of at least 6 months
      `I reasonably expected further employment`                                          IS A BOOLEAN @desc If casual: whether, apart from the employer's decision not to offer you more work, you had a reasonable expectation of further employment
      `the main purpose of my fixed engagement was to avoid unfair dismissal obligations` IS A BOOLEAN @desc If engaged for a specific period or task: whether the main purpose of engaging you that way was to avoid the employer's unfair dismissal obligations (a judgment the commission makes)
      `I am in a labour market program`                                                   IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether you were employed as a participant in a labour market program
      `I was dismissed before the period ended or the task was complete`                  IS A BOOLEAN @desc If engaged for a specific period or task: whether you were dismissed before the period ended or the task was complete
      `I am employed under an industrial instrument`                                      IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether an award, certified agreement or other industrial instrument covers your employment
      `I am a public service officer on tenure`                                           IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether you are a public service officer employed on tenure under the Public Sector Act 2022
      `my annual wages before the dismissal`                                              IS A NUMBER @desc Your annual wages immediately before the dismissal, in Australian dollars
      `the high income threshold`                                                         IS A NUMBER @desc The high income threshold under the Fair Work Act 2009 (Cwlth) s 333 at the time, in Australian dollars a year
      `my conduct`                                                                        IS A `Kind of conduct` @desc The conduct the employer relies on: theft, assault, sexual harassment or sex or gender based harassment, fraud, other misconduct prescribed by regulation, other conduct the employer calls misconduct, or no misconduct
      `I can show the conduct did not make continuing unreasonable`                       IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether you can show that, in the circumstances, the conduct did not make it unreasonable to continue your employment during the notice period
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`can I be dismissed without notice for misconduct` `the day my continuous service started` `the day my dismissal takes effect` `how I was engaged` `what was agreed about probation` `the agreed probation in months` `the longer probation is reasonable` `I was engaged regularly and systematically` `I was engaged for several periods over at least 6 months` `I reasonably expected further employment` `the main purpose of my fixed engagement was to avoid unfair dismissal obligations` `I am in a labour market program` `I was dismissed before the period ended or the task was complete` `I am employed under an industrial instrument` `I am a public service officer on tenure` `my annual wages before the dismissal` `the high income threshold` `my conduct` `I can show the conduct did not make continuing unreasonable` MEANS
    `the employer may dismiss without notice or compensation` (`my employment` `the day my continuous service started` `the day my dismissal takes effect` `an unused date` `how I was engaged` `what was agreed about probation` `the agreed probation in months` `the longer probation is reasonable` `I was engaged regularly and systematically` `I was engaged for several periods over at least 6 months` `I reasonably expected further employment` `the main purpose of my fixed engagement was to avoid unfair dismissal obligations` `I am in a labour market program` `I was dismissed before the period ended or the task was complete` `I am employed under an industrial instrument` `I am a public service officer on tenure` `my annual wages before the dismissal` `the high income threshold`) `my conduct` `I can show the conduct did not make continuing unreasonable`

@export By when must I apply for an order that my employer pay me the compensation it owed for dismissing me without notice (s 122(3))?
GIVEN `the day of the dismissal` IS A DATE @desc The day your dismissal took effect, ISO 8601
GIVETH A DATE
`last day to claim pay instead of notice` `the day of the dismissal` MEANS
    `the last day to claim notice compensation` `the day of the dismissal`

@export Am I owed redundancy pay under the Industrial Relations Act 2016 (Qld), and how much (ss 125-127)?
GIVEN `the day my continuous service started`                                             IS A DATE @desc The day your continuous service with this employer started, counting service with a former employer that the Act treats as service with this one (s 132), ISO 8601
      `the day my dismissal takes effect`                                                 IS A DATE @desc The day your dismissal took (or takes) effect, ISO 8601
      `how I was engaged`                                                                 IS A `Basis of engagement` @desc How you were engaged: on an ongoing basis, as a casual employee, by the hour or day, for a specific period or task, or for the duration of a particular season
      `what was agreed about probation`                                                   IS A `Probation agreement` @desc What you and your employer agreed in writing about probation: nothing, a shorter probation than 3 months, no probation, or (before you started) a longer probation
      `the agreed probation in months`                                                    IS A NUMBER @desc If you agreed a longer probation, how many months it was (otherwise 0)
      `the longer probation is reasonable`                                                IS A BOOLEAN @desc If you agreed a longer probation: whether it is a reasonable period for the nature and circumstances of the job (a judgment the commission makes; answer as you have been told or expect)
      `I was engaged regularly and systematically`                                        IS A BOOLEAN @desc If casual: whether this employer engaged you on a regular and systematic basis
      `I was engaged for several periods over at least 6 months`                          IS A BOOLEAN @desc If casual: whether you were engaged for several periods of employment over a period of at least 6 months
      `I reasonably expected further employment`                                          IS A BOOLEAN @desc If casual: whether, apart from the employer's decision not to offer you more work, you had a reasonable expectation of further employment
      `the main purpose of my fixed engagement was to avoid unfair dismissal obligations` IS A BOOLEAN @desc If engaged for a specific period or task: whether the main purpose of engaging you that way was to avoid the employer's unfair dismissal obligations (a judgment the commission makes)
      `I am in a labour market program`                                                   IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether you were employed as a participant in a labour market program
      `I was dismissed before the period ended or the task was complete`                  IS A BOOLEAN @desc If engaged for a specific period or task: whether you were dismissed before the period ended or the task was complete
      `I am employed under an industrial instrument`                                      IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether an award, certified agreement or other industrial instrument covers your employment
      `I am a public service officer on tenure`                                           IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether you are a public service officer employed on tenure under the Public Sector Act 2022
      `my annual wages before the dismissal`                                              IS A NUMBER @desc Your annual wages immediately before the dismissal, in Australian dollars
      `the high income threshold`                                                         IS A NUMBER @desc The high income threshold under the Fair Work Act 2009 (Cwlth) s 333 at the time, in Australian dollars a year
      `my employer no longer needs my job done by anyone`                                 IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether your employment ended because the employer no longer requires your job to be done by anyone
      `it was ordinary and customary turnover of labour`                                  IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether your employment ended because of the ordinary and customary turnover of labour
      `a regulation or my instrument excludes me from redundancy pay`                     IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether a regulation or your industrial instrument says the redundancy pay provisions do not apply to you
      `a substantial reason for my fixed engagement was to avoid redundancy pay`          IS A BOOLEAN @desc If engaged for a fixed period, task or season: whether a substantial reason for that was to avoid redundancy pay (a judgment)
      `the commission ordered a reduced amount`                                           IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether, on the employer's application, the commission has ordered your redundancy pay reduced (s 127)
      `the reduced amount ordered`                                                        IS A NUMBER @desc If so, the amount stated in the order, in Australian dollars (it may be 0); otherwise 0
      `my weekly pay for ordinary hours`                                                  IS A NUMBER @desc Your pay for a week of your ordinary hours, including allowances, loadings and penalties and other amounts under your contract, in Australian dollars
GIVETH A `Redundancy answer`
`what redundancy pay am I owed` `the day my continuous service started` `the day my dismissal takes effect` `how I was engaged` `what was agreed about probation` `the agreed probation in months` `the longer probation is reasonable` `I was engaged regularly and systematically` `I was engaged for several periods over at least 6 months` `I reasonably expected further employment` `the main purpose of my fixed engagement was to avoid unfair dismissal obligations` `I am in a labour market program` `I was dismissed before the period ended or the task was complete` `I am employed under an industrial instrument` `I am a public service officer on tenure` `my annual wages before the dismissal` `the high income threshold` `my employer no longer needs my job done by anyone` `it was ordinary and customary turnover of labour` `a regulation or my instrument excludes me from redundancy pay` `a substantial reason for my fixed engagement was to avoid redundancy pay` `the commission ordered a reduced amount` `the reduced amount ordered` `my weekly pay for ordinary hours` MEANS
    `the redundancy pay` (`my employment` `the day my continuous service started` `the day my dismissal takes effect` `an unused date` `how I was engaged` `what was agreed about probation` `the agreed probation in months` `the longer probation is reasonable` `I was engaged regularly and systematically` `I was engaged for several periods over at least 6 months` `I reasonably expected further employment` `the main purpose of my fixed engagement was to avoid unfair dismissal obligations` `I am in a labour market program` `I was dismissed before the period ended or the task was complete` `I am employed under an industrial instrument` `I am a public service officer on tenure` `my annual wages before the dismissal` `the high income threshold`) (`The redundancy` WITH `the employer no longer requires the job done by anyone` IS `my employer no longer needs my job done by anyone`, `the termination is ordinary and customary turnover of labour` IS `it was ordinary and customary turnover of labour`, `a regulation or instrument excludes the employee` IS `a regulation or my instrument excludes me from redundancy pay`, `a substantial reason for the fixed engagement was to avoid the division` IS `a substantial reason for my fixed engagement was to avoid redundancy pay`, `the commission ordered a reduced amount` IS `the commission ordered a reduced amount`, `the reduced amount ordered` IS `the reduced amount ordered`) `my weekly pay for ordinary hours`

§§ `General protections (ss 309-310)`
-- Situation: only if you have been dismissed or otherwise affected by a contravention of the general protections.

@export By when must I apply to the commission about a dismissal that breached the general protections (s 310(1))? Later, only if the commission finds exceptional circumstances.
GIVEN `the day of the dismissal` IS A DATE @desc The day your dismissal took effect, ISO 8601
GIVETH A DATE
`last day to apply about a general protections dismissal` `the day of the dismissal` MEANS
    `the last day to apply about a dismissal under the general protections` `the day of the dismissal`

@export By when must I apply to the commission about a general protections contravention other than dismissal (s 310(3))?
GIVEN `the day of the contravention` IS A DATE @desc The day the contravention (other than dismissal) happened, ISO 8601
GIVETH A DATE
`last day to apply about another contravention` `the day of the contravention` MEANS
    `the last day to apply about another general protections contravention` `the day of the contravention`

§§ `Unpaid wages and superannuation (ss 376, 378-379, 396, 475-477)`
-- Situation: only if you are owed wages or superannuation, or were overpaid.

@export By when must I apply to recover unpaid wages, a tool allowance or superannuation contributions (ss 379(3), 396(3), 476(4))? A child may claim as an adult would (s 378).
GIVEN `the day the amount became payable` IS A DATE @desc The day the unpaid wages, allowance or superannuation contribution became payable, ISO 8601
GIVETH A DATE
`last day to apply for unpaid wages` `the day the amount became payable` MEANS
    `the last day to apply for an unpaid amount` `the day the amount became payable`

@export If I apply on a given day, can this unpaid amount still be ordered paid to me (ss 379(4)(a), 396(4)(a), 475(1), 477(1))?
GIVEN `the day the amount became payable` IS A DATE @desc The day the unpaid wages, allowance or superannuation contribution became payable, ISO 8601
      `the day I apply`                   IS A DATE @desc The day you make (or will make) the application, ISO 8601
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`can this unpaid amount still be ordered` `the day the amount became payable` `the day I apply` MEANS
    `the unpaid amount can still be ordered` `the day the amount became payable` `the day I apply`

@export Where can I apply to recover my unpaid wages: a magistrate (s 379), the commission (claims of $100,000 or less, ss 475-476), or both?
GIVEN `the total amount I claim`                                      IS A NUMBER @desc The total amount you claim, in Australian dollars
      `I have already applied to a magistrate for the wages`          IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether you (or someone for you) have already applied to a magistrate under s 379 for the same matter
      `I have already applied to the commission for the wages`        IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether you (or someone for you) have already applied to the commission under s 475 for the same matter
      `I have already applied to a magistrate for the superannuation` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether an application has already been made to a magistrate under s 396 for the same matter
GIVETH A LIST OF `Forum for unpaid wages`
`where can I claim unpaid wages` `the total amount I claim` `I have already applied to a magistrate for the wages` `I have already applied to the commission for the wages` `I have already applied to a magistrate for the superannuation` MEANS
    `where an unpaid wages claim can be made` `the total amount I claim` `I have already applied to a magistrate for the wages` `I have already applied to the commission for the wages` `I have already applied to a magistrate for the superannuation`

@export Can my employer recover an overpayment by deducting it from my wages on a given day (s 376(2)-(3))?
GIVEN `the day I was overpaid`     IS A DATE @desc The day the employer paid you the amount you were not entitled to, ISO 8601
      `the day deductions started` IS A DATE @desc The day of the first deduction from your wages to recover it, ISO 8601
      `the day of this deduction`  IS A DATE @desc The day of the deduction you are asking about, ISO 8601
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`can my employer deduct the overpayment` `the day I was overpaid` `the day deductions started` `the day of this deduction` MEANS
    `the employer may deduct the overpayment from these wages` `the day I was overpaid` `the day deductions started` `the day of this deduction`
